I enter the doctor's room.
The doctor is sitting there.
He tells me to sit in the chair.
"What is the trouble?" the doctor asks.
"I do not feel well at all," I reply.
"I have a fever and a headache."
"What other problems do you have?" he asks.
"I have a bad sore throat," I say.
"When I drink water, my throat hurts a lot."
"Also, I have a heavy cough."
"Do you have body aches?" the doctor asks again.
"Yes, my whole body hurts," I say.
"Were you able to sleep at night?" he asks.
"No, I did not sleep because of the cough," I reply.
The doctor takes a small flashlight.
"Open your mouth," he tells me.
"Let me just check your throat."
I open my mouth.
He examines my throat.
